33. Search in Rotated Sorted Array

There is an integer array nums sorted in ascending order (with distinct values).
Prior to being passed to your function, nums is possibly left rotated at an unknown index k (1 <= k < nums.length) 
such that the resulting array is [nums[k], nums[k+1], ..., nums[n-1], nums[0], nums[1], ..., nums[k-1]] (0-indexed). 
For example, [0,1,2,4,5,6,7] might be left rotated by 3 indices and become [4,5,6,7,0,1,2].
Given the array nums after the possible rotation and an integer target, return the index of target if it is in nums, or -1 if it is not in nums.
You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.

Explanation:
1st find mid element and compare with target if it is it , return mid;
start the 2 pointer approach - first check left half is sorted,
if left half is sorted then check inside it if the inside left half is sorted by checjing the position of nums[left]<=target<=nums[mid].
  then shift right to mid-1
else 
  then shif left to mid+1
     this is done to eliminate the isider half.

similalry do for right half being sorted  nums[mid]<=target<=nums[right]
Code:

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int n=nums.length;
        int left=0; int right=n-1;

        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;

            if(nums[mid]==target){
                return mid;
            }

            // Check left half is sorted
            if(nums[left]<=nums[mid]){
                // Left half is sorted again?
                if(target<= nums[mid] && target>=nums[left]){
                    right=mid-1;
                }
                // Left half is not sorted , then
                else{
                    left=mid+1;
                }
            }
            
            // right half is sorted
            else{
                // Left half is sorted?
                if(target>nums[mid] && target<=nums[right]){
                    left=mid+1;
                }
                // left half is not sorted
                else{
                    right=mid-1;
                }
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
